    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390">

                <pb facs="0374" n="364" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg364"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/661: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Singapore</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Patton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Singapore</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-01T19:00:00+07:30">December 1, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 1—9:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>327. Governor today issued a proclamation declaring state of emergency and
                    calling out military, naval and air volunteer forces of Straits Settlements.
                    Military authorities issued statement at the <pb facs="0375" n="365"
                        xml:id="pg365"/> same time stressing that this does not signify immediate
                    deterioration of the situation but is only precautionary step permitting
                    mobilization to be effected without undue dislocation of civil activities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Patton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
